  "title": "RadarDINO: Distilling Visual Semantics into mmWave Radar for Human Mesh Reconstruction",
  "summary": "RadarDINO introduces a radar HMR framework that distills visual semantics from a DINOv3 teacher into 3D radar representations, providing voxel- and body-part-level supervision for part-aware radar representations. It outperforms existing methods on the M4Human dataset.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RadarDINO uses a DINOv3 teacher to transfer visual descriptors to radar voxels for improved supervision.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The method incorporates vertex- and joint-losses to directly constrain geometric reconstruction.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the M4Human dataset, it achieves performance improvements over the SOTA baseline across all evaluation splits.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
